Rem ==================================================================
Rem seedsinqtest.shoddy — test program for seedsinq.shoddy
Rem
Rem Assert-driven, in the seedsparsetest / seedtest pattern: it prints
Rem what it is doing and stops the run at the first assertion that
Rem fails, ending with ALL ASSERTIONS PASSED when it does not.
Rem
Rem THE GUARD LIST IS THE TEST LIST. Every refusal this seed can answer
Rem is walked below exactly once, and each is checked with Refuses,
Rem which asserts three things at a stroke: the word said no, it said
Rem why, and the session came through it with its stack and its
Rem arithmetic intact. Nothing typed at a prompt may end the session —
Rem the machine's Chunk ABORTS on a bad batch size and MinBy ABORTS on
Rem an empty list, so the seed has to catch both before they get there,
Rem and these are the assertions that prove it does.
Rem
Rem THE ORDERING TESTS DISCRIMINATE. The stability fixture pairs equal
Rem keys with distinguishable values and lists them in the opposite
Rem order to the answer, so a sort that merely inherited the input order
Rem fails here instead of passing by luck.
Rem
Rem Run: bin\mill run tst\seedsinqtest.shoddy   (from the repo root)
Rem ==================================================================

Include "../machines/cuttle.shoddy"
Include "../machines/reckoner.shoddy"
Include "../machines/seq.shoddy"
Include "../machines/str.shoddy"
Include "../machines/seeds/seedsinq.shoddy"
Include "../machines/seeds/seedbuiltin.shoddy"

Def Ran(st As RckState, line As String) As RckState
    Select Case RckEval(st, line)
        Case RckNext(st2, out)
            st2
        Case RckStop(st2, why, out)
            st2
        Case Else
            st

Def Bad(st As RckState, line As String) As Boolean
    Select Case RckEval(st, line)
        Case RckStop(st2, why, out)
            True
        Case Else
            False

Def Why(st As RckState, line As String) As String
    Select Case RckEval(st, line)
        Case RckStop(st2, why, out)
            why
        Case Else
            ""

Def Text(st As RckState) As String
    Join(Map(CutCells(RckStack(st)), Fn(c) => CutShow(c, RckFmt(st))), " | ")

Def Refuses(st As RckState, line As String, part As String) As Boolean
    Bad(st, line) And Instr(Why(st, line), part) > 0 And Text(Ran(st, line)) = Text(st) And Text(Ran(Ran(st, line), "1 1 +")) = Text(Ran(st, "1 1 +"))

Def Main()
    Let s0 = RckSeedBuiltin(RckSeedSinq(RckNew()))

    Print("--- the thirteen words are registered and carry their metadata ---")
    Assert(RckKnows(s0, "SORTBY") And RckKnows(s0, "SORTBYDESC") And RckKnows(s0, "GROUPBY"), "THE THREE THAT ORDER AND GATHER")
    Assert(RckKnows(s0, "MINBY") And RckKnows(s0, "MAXBY") And RckKnows(s0, "FINDFIRST"), "THE THREE THAT PICK ONE")
    Assert(RckKnows(s0, "TAKEWHILE") And RckKnows(s0, "SKIPWHILE"), "THE TWO THAT SLICE ON A CONDITION")
    Assert(RckKnows(s0, "DISTINCT") And RckKnows(s0, "UNION") And RckKnows(s0, "INTERSECT") And RckKnows(s0, "EXCEPT") And RckKnows(s0, "CHUNK"), "AND THE FIVE THAT NEED NO PROGRAM")
    Assert(All(RckDict(s0), Fn(e) => WordEffect(e) <> "" And WordDesc(e) <> ""), "NO WORD IS WITHOUT AN EFFECT LINE AND A DESCRIPTION")
    Assert(All(RckDict(s0), Fn(e) => Length(RckHelp(s0, WordName(e))) = 3), "AND HELP ANSWERS FOR EVERY ONE OF THEM")
    Rem Nothing here reads a file or draws anything, so nothing here may
    Rem claim to touch the world.
    Assert(All(RckDict(s0), Fn(e) => Instr(Lower(WordEffect(e)), "handle") = 0), "NO WORD'S EFFECT STRING MENTIONS A HANDLE")

    Print("--- SORTBY, with the empty program as the identity key ---")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, "{ 3 1 2 } [ ] SORTBY")) = "{ 1 2 3 }", "SORTBY ORDERS NUMBERS")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, "{ 3 1 2 } [ ] SORTBYDESC")) = "{ 3 2 1 }", "SORTBYDESC ORDERS THEM BACK")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, "{ } [ ] SORTBY")) = "{ }", "SORTBY OF NOTHING IS NOTHING")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, "{ 7 } [ ] SORTBY")) = "{ 7 }", "SORTBY OF ONE IS ITSELF")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, "{ 10 9 100 } [ ] SORTBY")) = "{ 9 10 100 }", "SORTBY IS NUMERIC, NOT LEXICAL")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, "{ \"pear\" \"apple\" \"fig\" } [ ] SORTBY")) = "{ \"apple\" \"fig\" \"pear\" }", "SORTBY ORDERS STRINGS TOO")

    Print("--- the key is what the program answers, not the element ---")
    Rem Ordered by remainder: the evens keep 2 before 4, the odds 1
    Rem before 3, which is the stability claim as well as the key claim.
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, "{ 1 2 3 4 } [ 2 MOD ] SORTBY")) = "{ 2 4 1 3 }", "SORTBY USES THE PROGRAM'S ANSWER AND KEEPS TIES IN ORDER")
    Rem Descending on the same key must move the groups and NOT the
    Rem members: a sort that reversed the whole list would say 3 1 4 2.
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, "{ 1 2 3 4 } [ 2 MOD ] SORTBYDESC")) = "{ 1 3 2 4 }", "SORTBYDESC MOVES THE GROUPS, NOT THE MEMBERS")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, "{ 1 2 3 } [ NEGATE ] SORTBY")) = "{ 3 2 1 }", "A COMPUTED KEY ORDERS BY ITSELF")

    Print("--- GROUPBY gathers into pairs of key and members ---")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, "{ 1 2 3 4 } [ 2 MOD ] GROUPBY")) = "{ ( 1 { 1 3 } ) ( 0 { 2 4 } ) }", "GROUPBY KEYS IN FIRST-SEEN ORDER, MEMBERS IN SOURCE ORDER")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, "{ } [ ] GROUPBY")) = "{ }", "GROUPBY OF NOTHING IS NOTHING")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, "{ 5 5 5 } [ ] GROUPBY")) = "{ ( 5 { 5 5 5 } ) }", "ONE KEY IS ONE GROUP")

    Print("--- MINBY, MAXBY and FINDFIRST ---")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, "{ 3 1 2 } [ ] MINBY")) = "1", "MINBY")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, "{ 3 1 2 } [ ] MAXBY")) = "3", "MAXBY")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, "{ 3 1 2 } [ NEGATE ] MINBY")) = "3", "MINBY ON A COMPUTED KEY")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, "{ 4 7 9 } [ 5 > ] FINDFIRST")) = "7", "FINDFIRST TAKES THE FIRST THE PROGRAM LIKES")

    Print("--- TAKEWHILE and SKIPWHILE ---")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, "{ 1 2 9 3 } [ 4 < ] TAKEWHILE")) = "{ 1 2 }", "TAKEWHILE STOPS AT THE FIRST FAILURE")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, "{ 1 2 9 3 } [ 4 < ] SKIPWHILE")) = "{ 9 3 }", "SKIPWHILE RESUMES THERE")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, "{ 9 1 } [ 4 < ] TAKEWHILE")) = "{ }", "TAKEWHILE CAN TAKE NOTHING")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, "{ 1 2 } [ 4 < ] SKIPWHILE")) = "{ }", "SKIPWHILE CAN SKIP EVERYTHING")

    Print("--- the five that need no program ---")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, "{ 3 1 3 2 1 } DISTINCT")) = "{ 3 1 2 }", "DISTINCT KEEPS THE FIRST SIGHTING")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, "{ 1 2 } { 2 3 } UNION")) = "{ 1 2 3 }", "UNION")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, "{ 1 2 3 } { 3 1 } INTERSECT")) = "{ 1 3 }", "INTERSECT KEEPS LEFT ORDER")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, "{ 1 2 3 } { 2 } EXCEPT")) = "{ 1 3 }", "EXCEPT")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, "{ 1 2 3 4 5 } 2 CHUNK")) = "{ { 1 2 } { 3 4 } { 5 } }", "CHUNK LEAVES A SHORT LAST BATCH")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, "{ } 3 CHUNK")) = "{ }", "CHUNK OF NOTHING IS NOTHING")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, "{ \"a\" \"b\" \"a\" } DISTINCT")) = "{ \"a\" \"b\" }", "DISTINCT ON STRINGS")

    Print("--- every refusal, and the session survives all of them ---")
    Assert(Refuses(s0, "7 [ ] SORTBY", "a LIST"), "SORTBY REFUSES A NUMBER WHERE THE LIST GOES")
    Assert(Refuses(s0, "{ 1 2 } 7 SORTBY", "a PROGRAM"), "SORTBY REFUSES A NUMBER WHERE THE PROGRAM GOES")
    Assert(Refuses(s0, "{ 1 2 } [ ] [ ] GROUPBY", "a LIST"), "GROUPBY REFUSES A PROGRAM WHERE THE LIST GOES")
    Rem A key that is neither a number nor a string cannot be ordered, so
    Rem it is refused by name rather than sorted by accident.
    Assert(Refuses(s0, "{ 1 2 } [ DROP { 1 } ] SORTBY", "a NUMBER, a STRING or a TRUE/FALSE key"), "SORTBY REFUSES A LIST AS A KEY")
    Assert(Refuses(s0, "{ } [ ] MINBY", "something in it"), "MINBY REFUSES AN EMPTY LIST INSTEAD OF ABORTING")
    Assert(Refuses(s0, "{ } [ ] MAXBY", "something in it"), "MAXBY REFUSES AN EMPTY LIST INSTEAD OF ABORTING")
    Assert(Refuses(s0, "{ 1 2 } [ 9 > ] FINDFIRST", "found nothing"), "FINDFIRST REFUSES A MISS INSTEAD OF INVENTING ONE")
    Assert(Refuses(s0, "{ 1 2 3 } 0 CHUNK", "1 or more"), "CHUNK REFUSES A ZERO BATCH INSTEAD OF NEVER FINISHING")
    Rem A negative never reaches the size guard: RckWholeArg turns it
    Rem away first, with its own wording. Both refusals are the seed's
    Rem job done — this asserts which one actually fires, so the day one
    Rem of them stops firing the test says which.
    Assert(Refuses(s0, "{ 1 2 3 } -1 CHUNK", "whole number of 0 or more"), "CHUNK REFUSES A NEGATIVE BATCH AT THE ARITY GUARD")
    Assert(Refuses(s0, "7 { 1 } UNION", "a LIST"), "UNION REFUSES A NUMBER ON THE LEFT")
    Assert(Refuses(s0, "{ 1 } 7 UNION", "a LIST"), "UNION REFUSES A NUMBER ON THE RIGHT")
    Assert(Refuses(s0, "7 DISTINCT", "a LIST"), "DISTINCT REFUSES A NUMBER")

    Print("--- a program may name a word the session defined a line earlier ---")
    Let s1 = Ran(s0, ": TENS 10 * ;")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s1, "{ 3 1 2 } [ TENS ] SORTBY")) = "{ 1 2 3 }", "A USER WORD WORKS AS A KEY PROGRAM")

    Print("ALL ASSERTIONS PASSED")
